menu "ToDoHelper: todo manager"

    config TODOHELPER_TODO_CACHE_FILE
        string "Cache file name under <app_dir>/cache"
        default "todos.json"
        help
            Written with the storage layer's two-slot protocol (X.new ->
            X.bak -> X), so a power loss can never take both the old and the
            new copy with it; the leftovers are reconciled at boot. The file
            lives in the *internal* LittleFS, not on the SD card, so swapping
            the card cannot make the list disappear (v1.5.0).

    config TODOHELPER_TODO_BACKUP_KEEP
        int "Number of daily backup files to keep in backup/"
        range 0 30
        default 7
        help
            0 disables backups. Backups never contain WiFi passwords, API keys
            or the auth token (requirement 8.8).

            NOTE (v1.5.0): this knob still drives no code - the dated
            backup/todos_YYYYMMDD.json series is NOT implemented yet. What
            protects the list today is the storage layer's generic X.bak slot
            (one generation back) plus the export/import HTTP routes, which
            hand the whole list to the user's computer. Implementing the dated
            series is on the v1.6.0 list; until then, do not advertise this
            option as a working feature.

endmenu
